  The ladder is read stepwise: a*dN improving means a per-electron energy baseline is the first thing missing; b*dN^2 improving further means charging curvature is also needed; h improving further means
  the correction depends on the configuration. What this says is which EXPRESSION is effective enough -- the fitted coefficients are not thereby identified as independent physical terms.

